  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD027239",
    "title": "Metabolic labeling of NMT substrates by photoactivatable/clickable myristate probes X3/X8/X10",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Efficiency of labelling by photoactivatable/clickable myristate probes X3/X8/X10 is compared to the positive control probe YnMyr. Additionally, negative controls for each probe were obtained by treatment with NMT ihibitor IMP-366 (DDD85464). The resulting data indicates efficient labeling of NMT substrates by photoactivatable probes that is NMT-dependent.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "SILAC heavy spike-in mixture was prepared as follows. HeLa cells passaged in R10K8 SILAC media supplemented with 10% FCS for at least 5 passages were treated in separate 10 cm tissue culture-treated dishes with YnMyr (5 μl), X3 (100 μl), X8 (100 μl), X10 (100 μl). After 24 h, cells were lysed and protein concentration measured. Equal amounts of proteins from all four conditions were mixed to create the spike-in.  HeLa cells in normal (light) media were treated with YnMyr (5 μl), X3 (100 μl), X8 (100 μl), X10 (100 μl) for 24 h with and without the addition of 0.5 μM of IMP-366 (DDD85646) NMT inhibitor, each treatment regime in triplicate. Cells were lysed and protein concentration measured. 250 μg of heavy spike-in was added to 250 μg of each lysate. Alkyne-tagged proteins were ligated to AzRB regent using Cu-catalyzed azide-alkyne cycloaddition.The lysates were enriched on streptavidin-agarose beads. Samples were reduced with TCEP, alkylated with IAA and digested with trypsin. The samples were desalted using STAGE-tipping. Peptides were separated on nano-LC column and detected using Thermo QExactive.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "RAW files were analysed using MaxQuant, using protein database for Homo sapiens (downloaded from UniProt). MaxQuant output file proteinGroups.txt was processed in Perseus.",
